Everything passes.

**logfan.go** — exports exactly the contract API:
- `NewRing(capacity)` — positive-capacity guard, `sync.RWMutex`-protected ring buffer, clones records on write, returns oldest-first copy on read
- `*Ring` implements `slog.Handler` (Enabled yes-all, Handle stores clone, WithAttrs/WithGroup return self — attrs already in record)
- `New(handlers...)` — empty-guard, delegates fan-out to `slog.NewMultiHandler`

**logfan_test.go** — 13 tests covering:
- Invalid capacity error (0, negative)
- Empty ring returns nil
- Capture order within capacity
- Single eviction and multiple-wrap eviction
- Records returns isolated copy
- Concurrent safety (race detector clean, 10 goroutines writing, 5 reading)
- New(no-handlers) error
- New sends to all handlers (two rings, same message in both)
- Compile-time `slog.Handler` interface check
- Enabled returns true for debug/info
- WithAttrs/WithGroup return *Ring
- Partial fill (non-wrapped) ordering
- Records are cloned (stored record unaffected by later Handle)

`go build ./...` ✓, `go vet ./...` ✓, `go test -race ./...` ✓
